Makes libass optional again (-Dlibass=disabled), against mpv v0.41.0.

tinystream renders text subtitles with rustyass, so its libmpv is built without libass. mpv made
libass mandatory in 0b9ed9c2 (2020) and removed the OSD stub it used without it. With libass
disabled:

- sd_ass (text subtitles) isn't built; sd_lavc (bitmap subtitles, like PGS) stays.
- sub/osd_dummy.c, brought back from before 0b9ed9c2 and updated to the current OSD interface in
  sub/osd.h and sub/osd_state.h, replaces osd_libass.c: the OSD draws nothing. It also defines
  sd_ass.c's (now empty) sub-filter options, which options.c refers to.
- The libass-version property is unavailable.

With libass enabled (the default), mpv builds as upstream does.

To refresh it for a new mpv: check out the new tag, apply this with `git apply --3way`, fix what
conflicts, check that osd_dummy.c still defines everything other files use from osd_libass.c and
sd_ass.c, update the version above, and write the result out with
`git diff > native/mpv/patches/no-libass.patch` (after `git add -N sub/osd_dummy.c`), keeping this
text at the top.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index fb10be5..46c80f0 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ libswscale = dependency('libswscale', version: '>= 7.5.100')
 libplacebo = dependency('libplacebo', version: '>=6.338.2',
                 default_options: ['default_library=static', 'demos=false'])
 
-libass = dependency('libass', version: '>= 0.12.2')
+libass = dependency('libass', version: '>= 0.12.2', required: get_option('libass'))
 
 # the dependency order of libass -> ffmpeg is necessary due to
 # static linking symbol resolution between fontconfig and MinGW
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ features = {
     'debug': get_option('debug'),
     'ffmpeg': true,
     'gpl': get_option('gpl'),
-    'libass': true,
+    'libass': libass.found(),
     'libplacebo': true,
 }
 
@@ -195,15 +195,12 @@ sources = files(
     'stream/stream_slice.c',
 
     ## Subtitles
-    'sub/ass_mp.c',
     'sub/dec_sub.c',
     'sub/draw_bmp.c',
     'sub/filter_sdh.c',
     'sub/img_convert.c',
     'sub/lavc_conv.c',
     'sub/osd.c',
-    'sub/osd_libass.c',
-    'sub/sd_ass.c',
     'sub/sd_lavc.c',
 
     ## Video
@@ -267,6 +264,12 @@ sources = files(
     'ta/ta_utils.c',
 )
 
+if features['libass']
+    sources += files('sub/ass_mp.c', 'sub/osd_libass.c', 'sub/sd_ass.c')
+else
+    sources += files('sub/osd_dummy.c')
+endif
+
 
 # compiler stuff
 cc = meson.get_compiler('c')
